  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and dizziness, raising concern for paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia. Given the history of transient cerebral ischemic attacks, prolonged ambulatory monitoring is indicated to correlate cardiac rhythm disturbances with these neurological symptoms and dizziness. Mobile cardiac telemetry monitoring (CPT 93229) is clinically necessary to detect and characterize the arrhythmia associated with the patient's symptoms, supporting diagnoses I47.1, G45.9, and R42."
